  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser TA riktat till finansiella institutioner (fr&#xe4;mst inom  SBBNs globala n&#xe4;tverk) i syfte att f&#xf6;rm&#xe5; dessa att i h&#xf6;gre grad rikta sin verksamhet mot sm&#xe5;f&#xf6;retag i utvecklingsekonomier.                  Programmet har tre komponenter: Kartl&#xe4;ggning, f&#xf6;rdjupat tekniskt     st&#xf6;d samt replikerbarhet/stordrift.                                    Gender och milj&#xf6; utg&#xf6;r tv&#xe4;rsektoriella aspekter inom programmet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution aims at develop and prove the business case for      financial institution in emerging economies to a higher degree adress SMEs.                                                                  The program uses a phased approach: diagnostics, on-site training    and replication/move to scale.                                         Gender and environment are importnt cross-cutting issues.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution aims at develop and prove the business case for financial institutions in emerging economies to a higher degree adress SMEs. The program uses a phased approach: diagnostics, on-site training and replication/move to scale. Gender and environment are important cross-cutting issues.
CapPlus conducts market assessments to be able to better serve low income clients and to ultimately select financial institution partners that are most willing and/or prepared to serve this market with integrity and scale, delivering impact where it is most needed. These market assessments are also exploration opportunities for the financial institutions, as they have a chance to learn more about best practice and potential that is &#x2018;out there&#x2019; in the field. It also helps catalyze more interest in financial inclusion for the poor, as key questions, challenges, market trends and opportunities are discussed.</narrative>
  </description>
